      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression confirmed by confocal microscopy and flow cytometry in HEK293 cells. Electrophysiological function not explicitly reported for the BBS-tagged construct in the cited papers, but robust surface trafficking was demonstrated. Multiple independent studies using HA tags in the same S1\u2013S2 loop (same protein, same loop) report no interference with processing or function (Akhavan et al. 2003, cited in PMC3861077).",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The ledger explicitly names T436/E437 as the insertion junction in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop (topology landmarks: EC 430\u2013453, flanked by TM S1 409\u2013429 and TM S2 454\u2013471). Python verification confirms full_seq[436]='T' and full_seq[437]='E', matching the paper exactly. Distance from S1 TM end (429): 7 residues; distance from S2 TM start (454): 18 residues \u2014 both well above the \u22653 residue minimum. The nearest disulfide-forming cysteines (C445, C449) are 9 and 13 residues downstream, respectively, leaving adequate spacing. The BBS tag (13 aa) is within the 13\u201323 aa target range; an ALFA tag with GS linkers (~19\u201321 aa) is similarly sized. Multiple independent papers confirm this loop tolerates epitope insertions without disrupting trafficking. A 13-residue bungarotoxin-binding site (BBS) was inserted between T436 and E437 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop of full-length hERG1a (also bearing a C-terminal YFP) in HEK293 cells. Surface expression of the intact membrane-anchored channel was confirmed by confocal microscopy (YFP total pool; BTX-Alexa647 surface pool) and flow cytometry (surface signals up to 100-fold above threshold). The construct is full-length and membrane-anchored; not a secreted ectodomain. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 29725305,
          "citation": "PMID 29725305",
          "claim": "A 13-residue bungarotoxin-binding site (BBS; TGGCGGTACTACGAGAGCAGCCTGGAGCCCTACCCCGAC) ( Sekine-Aizawa and Huganir, 2004 ; Yang et al., 2010 ) was then introduced between residues T436/E437 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop of hERG using the Quik-Change Lightning Site-Directed Mutagenesis Kit (Stratagene) according to the manufacturer's instructions. 16 LQT2 mutations were introduced in the PAS domain of BBS-hERG-YFP via site-directed mutagenesis."
        }
      ],
