      "tag_type": "short epitope, ALFA 15 aa, GS linkers (~19-21 aa total); analogous to HA tag with linkers (17 aa) validated here",
      "tag_length_aa": null,
      "linker": null,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Electrophysiological properties confirmed unaffected: 'This tag has been demonstrated previously not to affect the electrophysiological properties of the channel.' Stable expression construct validated for surface labeling. Function preserved.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The ledger explicitly names T443/E444 as the insertion junction in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop. Python verification confirms full_seq[443]='T' and full_seq[444]='E', matching the paper exactly. Distance from S1 TM end (429): 14 residues; distance from S2 TM start (454): 11 residues \u2014 both well above the \u22653 residue minimum. C445 is 2 residues downstream of the junction; however, the paper explicitly demonstrates electrophysiological function is preserved, indicating the insert does not disrupt the C445\u2013C449 disulfide. The HA-with-linkers insert (17 aa) is within the 13\u201323 aa target range; an ALFA tag with GS linkers is similarly sized. A second ledger line (PMC7704534) independently confirms HA tagging in the first extracellular loop of KV11.1/KCNH2 with surface expression validated by flow cytometry and confocal microscopy. A 9-amino acid HA tag with flanking 4-aa linkers (NSEHYPYDVPDYAVTFE, 17 aa total) was inserted between T443 and E444 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop of full-length KCNH2 (hERG1a) by inverse PCR. The construct was incorporated into a stable expression system (AttB-KCNH2-HA:IRES:mCherry). The paper explicitly states the tag does not affect electrophysiological properties of the channel. [validation: surface_and_function; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "citation": "preprint",
          "claim": "A previously published 34 9 amino acid HA tag with surrounding 4 amino acid linkers (NSEHYPYDVPDYAVTFE) was inserted between amino acids T443 and E444 (in the extracellular region between the S1 and S2 helices) by inverse PCR 35 (Table S1)."
        }
      ],
